# Downroad Design System

## Colours
Always use CSS variables. Never hardcode hex values.

| Variable | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--red-dark` | `#490504` | bg fills, pill backgrounds |
| `--red-bright` | `#E20000` | accents, active states, buttons |
| `--yellow-dark` | `#2E2200` | activity toast background |
| `--yellow-bright` | `#E8A800` | activity toast text & spinner |
| `--grey-muted` | `#A1A1A1` | placeholder, secondary text |
| `--white` | `#FFFFFF` | primary text |
| `--color-error` | `#FF453A` | error states & toasts |
| `--color-success` | `#30D158` | success states |
| `--color-warning` | `#FFD60A` | warning toasts |
| `--color-info` | `#FFFFFF` | info toasts |

## Typography
- Font: `Ligconsolata Bold` (monospace), 700 weight
- Base size: 14px. Scale: 11px meta · 12px chips · 13px secondary · 15px inputs · 18px headings

**Punctuation — strictly enforced:**
- ❌ Never use em dashes (`—`) anywhere in UI text
- ✅ Use `:` for label/continuation — e.g. `Ready: click Download`
- ✅ Use ` · ` to separate metadata — e.g. `1080p · MP4`
- ✅ Use `.` for sentence breaks
- ✅ Use `-` as a null/empty placeholder value

## Iconography
- **Only Hugeicons** (rounded stroke set). No emoji, no unicode symbols, no inline SVG.
- In JS: `icon('icon-name', 'ui-icon')` → renders `<i class="hgi-stroke hgi-{name}">`
- In HTML: `<i class="hgi-stroke hgi-{name} ui-icon">` + size modifier class

## Border Radius
- `--radius-pill: 45px` — URL bar, buttons, time inputs, quality bar
- `--radius-card: 18px` — video card, carousel card, toasts
- `--radius-sm: 10px` — queue items, small cards

## Spacing & Layout
- `--gap: 12px` — standard gap between stacked elements
- URL/controls width: 92%, max 900px, min 420px, centred

## Animation
- `--spring: cubic-bezier(0.32, 1.05, 0.36, 1)` — bouncy entrances
- `--ease: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1)` — smooth exits
- Animate with: `scale`, `translate`, `opacity`, `box-shadow` only
- ❌ No glow, no blur, no gradients on interactive elements

## Light Mode

### How it works
Light mode is driven by the `html.light-mode` class, applied by `applyTheme()` in `renderer.js`. The user can override via the Appearance toggle in Settings (dark / auto / light). All light-mode CSS lives at the bottom of `styles.css` under `html.light-mode` selectors — never scatter light-mode rules elsewhere, never use `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light)`.

### Core variable overrides (light)
| Variable | Light value | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `--red-dark` | `hsl(0, 68%, 80%)` | All dark pill/card backgrounds become warm pastel pink |
| `--grey-muted` | `hsl(0, 25%, 44%)` | Muted text stays readable on pink backgrounds |

### Project colours (light)
Each project has two extra colour tokens set via JS `projectColors()`:
| Token | Formula | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--proj-light-bg` | `hsl(hue, 60%, 72%)` | Pastel pill / card background |
| `--proj-light-text` | `hsl(hue, 72%, 28%)` | Dark saturated text on pastel bg |

### Light-mode component rules
| Component | Light treatment |
|---|---|
| **URL row** | Black-opacity border `rgba(0,0,0,0.75)` |
| **Download button** | Keeps `--red-bright` bg, forces `#fff` text (not `--red-dark`) |
| **Time inputs / Quality bar** | Brand red (`--red-dark` → pastel pink bg, `--red-bright` text) |
| **Quality bar active label** | `#fff` (sits on red pill indicator) |
| **Quality option text** | `--red-bright` |
| **Settings / Queue / Help popovers** | `--red-dark` → pastel pink bg; all `var(--white)` text overridden to `--red-bright` or `#111` |
| **Video card** | `--proj-subtle` tint bg; title falls back to `#111` when no project |
| **Carousel card** | `--red-dark` → pastel pink bg; title/count overridden to `#111` |
| **History view** | `rgba(245,245,245,0.97)` backdrop; entry cards use `--proj-light-bg` with `--proj-light-text` |
| **Activity toast** | `hsl(42,90%,88%)` bg, `hsl(42,100%,26%)` text (light amber) |
| **Status toasts** | Transparent tint of semantic colour (`rgba(R,G,B,0.13)`) |
| **Drop overlay** | `rgba(226,0,0,0.4)` semi-transparent scrim |
| **btn-hint** | `rgba(0,0,0,0.72)` dark pill with white text |
| **Scrollbars** | `rgba(0,0,0,0.2)` global; `rgba(0,0,0,0.15)` history list |
| **Project pill** | `--proj-light-bg` bg, `--proj-light-text` text |
| **Active filter / menu item** | `--proj-light-bg` bg, `--proj-light-text` text |

### Rules
- ✅ All light overrides use `html.light-mode .selector { }` prefix
- ✅ Multi-selector rules must prefix EVERY selector with `html.light-mode`
- ❌ Never use `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light)` — the class handles both auto and manual
- ❌ Never hardcode `rgba(255,255,255,X)` subtle backgrounds in light mode — use `rgba(0,0,0,X)`
- ❌ Never use `color: var(--white)` on elements that sit on `--red-dark` backgrounds in light mode

## Truncation

**Always use middle truncation** — never end-truncation for user-facing title/content strings. This mirrors macOS Finder's `NSLineBreakByTruncatingMiddle` behaviour: showing the start (what it is) and the end (episode number, qualifier, file extension) with `…` in the middle.

**Two utilities** in `renderer.js` — use the right one for the context:
- `midTruncate(str, maxLen)` — character-count based, for fixed-width contexts (dialogs, stored titles)
- `observeQueueTitle(el, fullTitle)` — pixel-accurate, ResizeObserver + canvas measurement for dynamic-width elements like queue cards. Automatically re-truncates on every resize. Pair with `unobserveQueueTitle(el)` on removal.

```js
// 58% front · … · 35% tail — matches Apple's Finder split ratio
function midTruncate(str, maxLen = 65) {
  if (!str || str.length <= maxLen) return str;
  const tail = Math.floor(maxLen * 0.35);
  const head = maxLen - tail - 1;
  return str.slice(0, head) + '…' + str.slice(-tail);
}
```

**Character budgets by context:**

| Context | Budget | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Queue item titles | 65 | Standard queue width |
| History list / grid card titles | 65 | Same |
| History compact row titles | 50 | Narrower layout |
| Cancel / delete dialog subtitles | 55–60 | Fixed-width dialogs |
| Instagram caption display titles | 80 | Wider header area |
| File paths | n/a | Use `truncatePath()` instead — Apple path-component style |

**Rules:**
- ✅ For **dynamic-width elements** (queue cards): use `observeQueueTitle(el, fullTitle)` after inserting the element — never put a pre-truncated string in the template
- ✅ For **fixed-width contexts** (dialogs, history titles): use `midTruncate(str, maxLen)` before inserting, wrapped with `escapeHtml()`: `${escapeHtml(midTruncate(title, 65))}`
- ✅ Call `unobserveQueueTitle(el.querySelector('.queue-item__title'))` before removing any queue item from the DOM
- ✅ Keep CSS `text-overflow: ellipsis` on truncated elements as a last-resort safety fallback
- ❌ Never use `.slice(0, N) + '…'` for any visible UI string — that is end-truncation
- ❌ Do NOT apply `midTruncate()` to short badge labels (project pills, quality chips, channel names in chips) — end-truncation via CSS is correct there
- ❌ Do NOT apply `midTruncate()` to data-layer strings stored to DB (captions, descriptions, stderr)

## Key Components
- **URL Row** — white 2px border pill, `background: transparent`, max 900px
- **Download button** — red pill inside URL row, 10px inset margin, 38px tall
- **Time inputs** — `--red-dark` pill, inset box-shadow ring (green = has value, red = error)
- **Quality bar** — `--red-dark` pill, sliding red pill indicator
- **Activity toast** — `--yellow-dark` bg, `--yellow-bright` text, fixed bottom-centre
- **Status toast** — `--red-dark` bg, coloured text, max 520px, copy button on errors
- **Sticker** — 220×220px, `object-fit: contain`, pop animation on swap
